#!/bin/sh
# Installs Incipit on this Mac for its user: builds the bundle from this checkout with
# tools/package-mac and puts it at ~/Applications/Incipit.app, in place of the copy there. Run it
# again to install the checkout as it is now.
#
#   tools/setup            once: pdfium's library, which goes inside the bundle
#   tools/install-mac
#
# The copy is the bundle the disk image holds, so it is what a learner gets. macOS does not ask to
# allow it, because it was built here: only a downloaded file carries the mark that makes it ask.
# The user's own Applications folder needs no administrator's password. The bundle is registered
# with Launch Services, so Launchpad and "Open With" know it at once, not after the next scan.
#
# The new copy is made beside the old one and checked before the old one goes, so a failed build
# or copy leaves the installed app as it was. The script refuses, changing nothing, while the
# installed copy is running (the old program would go on from deleted files; quit it first), and
# when ~/Applications/Incipit.app is some other app (its identifier is not Incipit's).
set -eu
. "$(dirname "$0")/package-common"

[ "$(uname -s)" = Darwin ] || package_fail "this installs the macOS app and runs on a Mac"
folder="$HOME/Applications"
installed="$folder/Incipit.app"
built="$package_out/Incipit.app"
identifier=$(package_identifier)
lsregister=/System/Library/Frameworks/CoreServices.framework/Frameworks/LaunchServices.framework/Support/lsregister

# Checked before the build, so a running app is said at once, and again after it, since the build
# takes minutes and the app may have been started meanwhile.
refuse_if_running() {
    if pgrep -f "^$installed/Contents/MacOS/incipit" >/dev/null; then
        package_fail "Incipit is running from $installed; quit it (⌘Q) and run this again"
    fi
}

if [ -e "$installed" ]; then
    found=$(plutil -extract CFBundleIdentifier raw -o - "$installed/Contents/Info.plist" 2>/dev/null || true)
    [ "$found" = "$identifier" ] ||
        package_fail "$installed is not Incipit (its identifier is '${found:-none}', not $identifier); move it away first"
fi
refuse_if_running

"$package_root/tools/package-mac"

refuse_if_running
mkdir -p "$folder"
# A folder beside the installed app, on the same disk, so putting the new copy in place is a rename.
stage=$(mktemp -d "$folder/.incipit-install.XXXXXX")
trap 'rm -rf "$stage"' EXIT
ditto "$built" "$stage/Incipit.app"
codesign --verify --strict "$stage/Incipit.app"
rm -rf "$installed"
mv "$stage/Incipit.app" "$installed"
"$lsregister" -f "$installed"

echo
echo "Installed:  $installed (version $(package_version), $(package_size "$installed"))"
echo "Open it from Launchpad, Spotlight or the Finder."
